Subject: [PATCH 04/12] itasha: an Auto Decoration dialog - family, motif, base
 paint and name text in one place

The scattered entries (Grow Decoration, Motif Family, Base Paint, and the
composition family and name text the engine grew) become one dialog.
Opening it reads the project's recipe (flsedit state) so it shows the
current choices; Compose sends everything at once to the "decorate"
action - composition family, motif family, base paint (from the design or
a picked colour) and the optional character name text (name, title,
style, placement, priority, outline, shadow, layer cap, game-font
fallback) - and switches the decoration on. Drop Decoration stays. The
last text input is also kept in QSettings itasha/text/*. Strings go to
the engine as single QProcess arguments, so spaces and case survive.
Korean entries for every new string.
